  .sb-arts-foot {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-12);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* ── The chat handoff ──
     THE SAME PANEL AS THE TWO SUGGESTION STRIPS, because it is the third thing this form says in
     its own voice rather than the visitor's, and three shapes for one idea would make the reader
     work out whether they differ.

     ALL OF THIS IS SERVER-RENDERED AND ONLY TOGGLED, which is the whole reason it is markup here
     and not a string built at click time. A scoped `<style>` never reaches a node the browser made
     after render — the defect that left every chat message unstyled for the life of the old chat
     page — so the only thing `lib/submit.ts` writes into this block is the VALUE of a textarea.
     There is no class here that a runtime node has to carry. */
  .sb-hand {
    margin-top: -4px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-8);
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
  }

  /* An author `display` beats the `hidden` attribute, and this block has one. */
  .sb-hand[hidden] { display: none; }

  .sb-hand-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

