     receipt alone because this is the screen where somebody decides whether to press send, and
     the second sentence is what turns silence about how long into a stated policy. */
  .sb-hand-wait {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-12);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* ── Duplicate suggestions ── */
  .sb-dupes {
    margin-top: -4px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-8);
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
  }

  .sb-dupes[hidden] { display: none; }

  .sb-dupes-h {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-13);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
  }

  .sb-dupes :global(.sb-dupe) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 8px;
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-6);
  }

  .sb-dupes :global(.sb-dupe + .sb-dupe) { border-top: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300); }
  .sb-dupes :global(.sb-dupe-title) { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: var(--bo-t-14); }
  .sb-dupes :global(.sb-dupe-title a) { color: var(--sl-color-text-accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sb-dupes :global(.sb-dupe-title a:hover) { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ── The three desks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* NEITHER RED NOR AMBER, AND NOT A FIFTH HUE EITHER. Red on this page means something broke, and
     neither an invoice question nor a pre-sales question is a fault. Amber is spoken for by the
     public-board warning, the one thing here that must not be missed. That much was already
     settled when billing and the catch-all took the neutral surface.

     Sales was the case for reaching past those two. It was refused. The tint on this grid does not
     encode TOPIC, it encodes what happens to what you write: red says a fault, blue says this
     becomes public, and neutral says neither. Sales is neither, so neutral is not a leftover for
     it, it is the correct answer. The two hues left unused are both worse than correct — green
     already means "shipped, this exists" on the roadmap board this page links to and shares status
     tokens with, and blue is the public lane, which is the one thing a private door must not
     suggest. A fifth hue would also make three of five tiles shout, and the fork would stop being
     two lanes and three desks and become five competing offers.

     What tells a stranger this door is theirs is the label, the handshake and the first three
     words of the body, which is where that work belongs. Sharing one tint is what makes the bottom
     row read as three desks rather than as three more lanes. */
  .sb-choice-icon-admin {
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
  }

  /* ── Attachments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .sb-files {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .sb-files-h { font-size: var(--bo-t-14); font-weight: 500; }

