     with 20px hanging below it centres as a 52.8px box and the visible part rides 10px — exactly
     half the margin — above the line. The same 20px was also inflating the row: 32.8 + 20 + 16 of
     padding is the 68.8 measured, where the row's own content needs 48.8.

     WHERE IT CAME FROM. The prose-rhythm reset at the top of this sheet lists nine containers whose
     direct children get `margin-top: 0`, and this button is not a direct child of any of them — it
     is inside a row `lib/submit.ts` writes at runtime. So it kept a margin meant for stacked prose.
     `margin: 0` states it on the control itself, which is where a control's box belongs. */
  .sb-file-list :global(.sb-file-drop) {
    flex: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-4);
    background: none;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-13);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 150ms ease-out, color 150ms ease-out, border-color 150ms ease-out;
  }

  .sb-file-list :global(.sb-file-drop-ic) {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: none;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ── RED ON INTENT, NOT AT REST — and the reason is a named rule, not taste ────────────────────
     Oleh asked for red, "або хоча б іконку". It gets both, in that order, because DESIGN.md §2's
     Red-Means-Broken Rule is explicit: Fault Red is "**Never** used for a decision, a rejection, or
     an unavailable option; only for something that went wrong." Detaching a file you attached ten
     seconds ago, before anything is sent, is a decision, and it is undone by picking the file again.
     A row that paints it red says a mistake has happened when none has — and with the five-file
     limit this form allows, five permanently red buttons is the column of alarms the same document
     bans for status pills.

