     sentence. Two separate regions would queue and interrupt each other, and putting the list
     itself in one would read every row aloud on every change. */
  .sb-file-live {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .sb-file-count { margin: 0; font-size: var(--bo-t-12); color: var(--bo-muted); }

  /* A REFUSED FILE IS NOT A CATASTROPHE. Nothing broke, so nothing here is red — on this page red
     means a backup failed. Amber is the "read this before you continue" tone, and it cannot collide
     with the public-board warning that owns it, because that warning lives on the one form with no
     file input: the two can never appear on the same screen. */
  .sb-file-note {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 8px 12px;
